The minor in which a proof says what it assumes, counts only what it should, and an agent can ask a person its own question. It carries the primes trial's fixes:
- a proof counts what it should (#763);
- a proof says what it assumes and asks: assumed and discharges, generalizations over declared variables, stated independence, statement_kind, ask_question and the design-a-proof skill (#764);
- corollary and proposition as statement kinds (#765).

